{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"a994bafa438a18e7","type":"text","text":"\"What is it?\" Lilith asked. She knew that look: he had something not socially comfortable to say. \n\n\"It's... It's rather odd.\" He warned.\n\n\"Then you simply must tell me, please?\" She was rather curious. \n\n- [ ] she's often open to his thoughts that he thinks are less socially acceptable\n\nHe whispered in her ear, \"There's a part of me that wishes... you were pregnant.\" \n\nShe supposed in a way it was a fitting irony. \"Your parents would never accept a child conceived out of wedlock.\" As they both knew it was the truth of the matter. \n\nHe sighed, \"I know. I suppose I find myself wanting children.\" Alex rested his hands on her belly.\n\nLilith would miss his touch when she broke things off before her womb was swollen from the child she carried. \"With anyone in particular, or is it a more general feeling?\"\n\n\"I'm not sure. There's this one, my parents introduced us not long ago. She's new money, but I think she might actually be interested in me. I'm not totally sure yet though.\" \n\n\"Well, only way to know is to give it time.\" She put her hands over his, repeating his own words back to him.\n\nHe looked down at her and smirked. \"How clever, a witty remark for sure.\" he repeated hers back at her, then leaned in to kiss her.\n\nShe let her tongue explore his mouth and they both moaned. This was indeed a temporary season, though it was rather fun. Maybe when her child was grown, she would date another human. If she found one charming enough.","x":-340,"y":-300,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c6bcb9efb4c1baf7","type":"text","text":"That was something they had discussed before. Sometimes it was hard to tell rather a woman was interested in the Goth name or the Goth fortune. It was often some combination of the two when it was a woman he parents had introduced him to.\n\n\"Well, there's only one way I've found to find out.\"\n\n\"And that is?\"\n\n----\n\n\"She seems nice.\" He frowned. \n\nLilith raised an eyebrow, \"And?\"\n\n\"So many of them do, and generally all they are actually interested in is my family's name or my family's wealth.\" He said. \"No matter how much they act interested in me.\" \n\n\"How do you tell\" \n\n\"Well, only way to know is to give it time.\" Alex tisked. ","x":-880,"y":-340,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"61a0b70c95286fd8","x":260,"y":-300,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"Like if Alex is aware enough to realize he got this space to figure out what he wanted with his life, then would he wonder what Lilith got out of it. Obviously he doesn't know she got her daughter. \n\nHer smile was knowing, yet motherly, \"There is no need for you to concern yourself with that. I have gotten plenty from out time together.\"\n"},
		{"id":"de42ec3259e66ddb","x":260,"y":-700,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"Idk. If he does offer her any money, she won't take it. \n\n\"Are you sure? It's not enough for anyone in my family to notice.\"\n\n\"I appreciate that you want to ensure I have the resources I need, but I assure you, I have no need for your family's money. I have enough of my own for my needs and desires.\" \n\nI mean idk if I want to include that, but like I said, even if he does offer, she won't take it. She honestly doesn't need it. And not because her family is old money the way his is, she's old enough that she's earned enough that she just has money. "}
	],
	"edges":[]
}